INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_26',
  'A development team is building a new microservices application and wants to ensure that individual components can fail without affecting the entire system. They need to design the architecture so that each service can scale independently and communicate asynchronously. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar is most directly addressed by this approach?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence, which focuses on running and monitoring systems to deliver business value.","Security, which focuses on protecting information, systems, and assets.","Reliability, which focuses on the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions.","Performance Efficiency, which focuses on using computing resources efficiently to meet system requirements."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The Reliability pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on the ability of a system to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. Designing for failure, decoupling components, and enabling independent scaling are core principles of reliability. Option A focuses on operations. Option B focuses on protection. Option D focuses on resource utilization. While all are important, reliability directly addresses the system''s ability to withstand and recover from failures.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_27',
  'A company is building a new application that processes customer orders. They want to ensure that if one part of the order processing system fails (e.g., inventory check), it does not bring down the entire order placement process. They need to isolate failures and allow components to operate independently. Which AWS Cloud design principle should they prioritize?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement elasticity, allowing the system to scale resources up and down automatically based on demand.","Design for failure, ensuring that the system can gracefully degrade and recover from unexpected outages.","Decouple components, using queues or messaging services to separate interdependent parts of the application.","Think parallel, distributing processing tasks across multiple compute resources to improve throughput."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Decoupling components is a design principle that involves separating different parts of an application so they can operate independently. This prevents cascading failures, allows components to scale independently, and improves overall system resilience, directly addressing the need to isolate failures in the order processing system. Option A focuses on dynamic scaling. Option B is a broader principle of resilience, but decoupling is a specific mechanism. Option D focuses on performance. While all are design principles, decoupling directly addresses fault isolation between components.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_28',
  'A company wants to improve its operational efficiency by automating routine tasks such as infrastructure provisioning, configuration management, and deployment. They aim to reduce manual effort, minimize human error, and accelerate the release cycle. Which AWS Cloud design principle is most relevant to this objective?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure, focusing on building resilient systems that can withstand component failures.","Decouple components, separating services to prevent cascading failures and allow independent scaling.","Implement elasticity, allowing systems to automatically scale resources up or down based on demand.","Automate everything, using tools and scripts to eliminate manual processes and ensure consistency."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Automate everything is a core design principle in the AWS Cloud, emphasizing the use of automation for provisioning, configuration, deployment, and operational tasks. This reduces manual effort, minimizes errors, and accelerates the release cycle, directly aligning with the goal of improving operational efficiency. Option A focuses on resilience. Option B focuses on fault isolation. Option C focuses on dynamic scaling. While these are valid principles, automation directly addresses the streamlining of routine tasks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_29',
  'A company wants to ensure its critical application can automatically recover from infrastructure failures, such as an Amazon EC2 instance crash, without manual intervention. They need to design the system to be self-healing and resilient. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar primarily focuses on this capability?',
  'mcq',
  '["Security","Reliability","Performance Efficiency","Cost Optimization"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The Reliability pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to. This includes the ability to recover from infrastructure or service disruptions, dynamically acquire computing resources to meet demand, and mitigate disruptions such as misconfigurations or transient network issues. Security (Option 0) focuses on protecting information. Performance Efficiency (Option 2) focuses on using resources efficiently. Cost Optimization (Option 3) focuses on minimizing expenses.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_30',
  'An application experiences varying traffic patterns throughout the day, with peak usage during business hours and minimal usage overnight. The company wants to automatically adjust its compute capacity to match demand, ensuring optimal performance while minimizing costs. Which design principle should be applied?',
  'mcq',
  '["Design for failure","Decouple components","Implement elasticity","Think parallel"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Implementing elasticity is a design principle that involves designing systems to automatically scale resources up or down based on demand. This allows the application to handle varying traffic patterns efficiently, ensuring optimal performance during peaks and cost savings during off-peak times. Design for failure (Option 0) is about resilience. Decouple components (Option 1) is about architectural independence. Think parallel (Option 3) is about concurrent processing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_31',
  'A company is building a new application and wants to ensure that all infrastructure components, such as Amazon EC2 instances, Amazon S3 buckets, and Amazon RDS databases, are provisioned and managed in a consistent and repeatable manner. They want to avoid manual configuration and ensure version control for their infrastructure. Which concept supports this approach?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating servers as pets","Building tightly coupled architectures","Benefits of disposable resources and infrastructure as code","Deploying to a single Availability Zone"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The benefits of disposable resources and infrastructure as code (IaC) directly support this approach. IaC allows infrastructure to be defined in code, enabling consistent, repeatable, and version-controlled provisioning. Disposable resources mean that instances can be easily replaced rather than manually maintained. Treating servers as pets (Option 0) is an anti-pattern that contradicts IaC. Building tightly coupled architectures (Option 1) is an anti-pattern for resilience. Deploying to a single Availability Zone (Option 3) is an anti-pattern for high availability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_32',
  'A team is developing a critical business application that requires maximum uptime. They are concerned about potential outages affecting their application if it''s deployed in only one physical location. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework pillar should guide their design to ensure the application can withstand failures?',
  'mcq',
  '["Operational Excellence","Security","Reliability","Cost Optimization"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The Reliability pillar focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to. This includes designing systems that can recover from infrastructure failures, which is crucial for maximizing uptime and withstanding outages. Operational Excellence (Option 0) focuses on running and monitoring systems. Security (Option 1) focuses on protecting information. Cost Optimization (Option 3) focuses on minimizing expenses.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

