INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_26',
  'A rapidly growing startup is launching a new social media application and anticipates highly variable user traffic. They expect significant spikes during promotional events and quiet periods otherwise. The development team needs to ensure the application can handle these unpredictable load changes automatically, scaling resources up and down as needed, to avoid performance issues during peak times and minimize infrastructure costs during off-peak hours. Which fundamental benefit of AWS Cloud computing directly addresses this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Elasticity, allowing resources to automatically scale based on demand.","Global infrastructure, enabling deployment to multiple regions for low latency.","High availability, ensuring the application remains operational even with component failures.","Economies of scale, providing lower pricing due to AWS''s large customer base."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Elasticity is the ability to acquire resources as you need them and release them when you no longer need them. This directly addresses the startup''s need to handle unpredictable traffic spikes by automatically scaling resources up and down, ensuring optimal performance and cost efficiency. Option 1 (Global infrastructure) is a benefit but focuses on geographic distribution and latency, not dynamic capacity adjustment. Option 2 (High availability) ensures continuous operation but does not specifically address the dynamic scaling of resources based on fluctuating demand. Option 3 (Economies of scale) is a cost benefit of AWS but describes a pricing advantage rather than the operational mechanism for handling variable load.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_27',
  'A rapidly growing startup is launching a new social media application and expects highly unpredictable user traffic patterns, including sudden, massive spikes during viral events or marketing campaigns. The development team needs to frequently deploy updates and new features, requiring an infrastructure that can adapt quickly to changing demands without significant manual intervention. The company''s primary goal is to minimize initial capital expenditure and avoid paying for idle resources, while ensuring the application remains responsive during peak loads. Which core benefit of the AWS Cloud directly addresses these requirements?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to deploy infrastructure globally in minutes, ensuring low latency for users worldwide.","Elasticity, enabling automatic scaling of resources based on demand, with a pay-as-you-go model.","Massive economies of scale, which guarantee that AWS will always be cheaper than any on-premises solution.","High availability and fault tolerance, ensuring that the application can withstand failures within a single Availability Zone."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option 1 (Elasticity) is correct because it directly addresses the startup''s need for an infrastructure that can automatically scale with unpredictable traffic and the desire to pay only for consumed resources, minimizing idle capacity costs and capital expenditure. This is a fundamental benefit of cloud computing. Option 0 (Global deployment) is a benefit of AWS but does not directly address the scaling and cost-efficiency for unpredictable traffic. Option 2 (Economies of scale) is a benefit, but it does not guarantee that AWS will *always* be cheaper than on-premises, especially if resources are over-provisioned or always on (anti-pattern ap-1.1-001). Option 3 (High availability and fault tolerance) is a critical design principle but doesn''t specifically address the agility, elasticity, and cost-saving aspects of scaling with variable demand.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_28',
  'A global e-commerce company plans to expand its online presence to new markets across different continents. They require their applications to be highly available and provide low-latency access to customers worldwide. The company wants to achieve this expansion quickly without the significant upfront capital expenditure and time associated with building new physical data centers in each region. They are looking for a solution that allows them to deploy their services closer to their international customer base efficiently.',
  'mcq',
  '["Deploy all application components within a single AWS Region and use a Content Delivery Network (CDN) to cache static content globally, assuming most users will tolerate higher latency for dynamic requests.","Invest in dedicated private network links to each new country, managing all network infrastructure directly.","Utilize AWS Regions and Availability Zones to deploy applications geographically closer to users.","Purchase and maintain physical servers in co-location facilities in each target country to reduce data transfer costs and ensure local data residency."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The benefit of AWS global infrastructure is the ability to deploy applications across multiple AWS Regions and Availability Zones, bringing services closer to end-users for low latency and high availability without the capital expenditure of building physical data centers. Option 2 directly addresses this by leveraging AWS''s global infrastructure. Option 0 would result in higher latency for users far from the single region and doesn''t fully address global reach for dynamic content. Option 1 and Option 3 involve significant upfront capital expenditure and operational overhead, which the company wants to avoid, contradicting the benefits of cloud computing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_29',
  'A rapidly growing startup is launching a new global social media application. They anticipate highly unpredictable user traffic, with potential for sudden, massive spikes during viral events, followed by periods of lower activity. The company needs to ensure their infrastructure can automatically adjust to these fluctuations without manual intervention, while only paying for the resources consumed. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud directly addresses this core requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Economies of scale, reducing the cost per unit as usage grows.","High availability, ensuring the application remains accessible during outages.","Elasticity, allowing automatic scaling of resources up or down based on demand.","Global infrastructure, enabling deployment of services closer to users worldwide."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Elasticity is the ability to acquire resources as you need them and release them when you no longer need them. This allows the startup to automatically scale compute capacity up during traffic spikes and scale down during quieter periods, ensuring they only pay for what they use and avoid over-provisioning. Economies of scale (Option 0) are a cost benefit, not a direct solution for automatic capacity adjustment. High availability (Option 1) focuses on uptime and fault tolerance, not dynamic scaling. Global infrastructure (Option 3) relates to geographic reach and latency, not automatic resource adjustment based on demand.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_30',
  'A traditional enterprise is considering migrating its on-premises data center to the AWS Cloud. They currently incur significant upfront capital expenditures for purchasing servers, storage, and networking equipment every few years. The finance department is looking for a way to shift these large, infrequent expenses to a more predictable, operational cost model that aligns with actual usage. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud directly supports this financial objective?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to deploy globally in minutes, enhancing market reach.","The benefit of massive economies of scale, leading to lower pricing.","Trading capital expenditure (CapEx) for variable expenditure (OpEx).","Increased speed and agility in provisioning new resources for development teams."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'One of the primary financial benefits of the AWS Cloud is the ability to trade capital expenditure (CapEx) for variable expenditure (OpEx). Instead of investing heavily in data centers and servers before you know how you''ll use them, you can pay only when you consume computing resources, and pay only for how much you consume. Deploying globally (Option 0) is an operational benefit, not a financial model shift. Economies of scale (Option 1) contribute to cost savings but don''t define the CapEx to OpEx shift. Increased speed and agility (Option 3) are operational benefits for development, not a financial model change.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_31',
  'A company operates an internal analytics application that experiences predictable peak usage during business hours and minimal activity overnight and on weekends. They are currently running this application on dedicated on-premises servers, which are often underutilized outside of peak times. The company wants to move this application to AWS to optimize costs by only paying for the compute resources when they are actively needed. Which core benefit of the AWS Cloud directly supports this cost optimization goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["The enhanced security posture provided by AWS global infrastructure.","The ability to stop guessing capacity and scale resources on demand.","The benefit of massive economies of scale, reducing the overall cost of services.","The increased fault tolerance and high availability across multiple Availability Zones."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The ability to stop guessing capacity allows customers to provision exactly the right amount of resources needed at any given time, and scale up or down as demand changes. This directly enables the company to pay only for the compute resources when the application is actively used, aligning with the pay-as-you-go model and optimizing costs. Enhanced security (Option 0) is a benefit but not the primary one for this specific cost optimization. Economies of scale (Option 2) contribute to lower pricing generally, but ''stopping guessing capacity'' specifically addresses the dynamic resource allocation for cost savings in this scenario. Increased fault tolerance (Option 3) is a reliability benefit, not directly related to optimizing costs for fluctuating usage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_32',
  'A software development firm is looking to accelerate its product release cycles. Their current on-premises infrastructure requires weeks to provision new development and testing environments, significantly delaying new feature deployment. They want to adopt a cloud strategy that allows their developers to quickly spin up and tear down environments in a matter of minutes, enabling rapid experimentation and faster time-to-market. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud best supports this objective?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to achieve massive economies of scale, lowering infrastructure costs.","The benefit of high availability, ensuring applications remain operational during failures.","Increased speed and agility, allowing rapid provisioning of resources.","The capability to deploy applications globally in minutes, reaching a wider audience."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Increased speed and agility refers to the ability to quickly provision and de-provision resources, allowing development teams to experiment more freely and deploy applications faster. This directly addresses the firm''s need to accelerate release cycles by reducing environment provisioning time from weeks to minutes. Economies of scale (Option 0) are a cost benefit. High availability (Option 1) is a reliability benefit. Deploying globally (Option 3) is a geographic reach benefit. While all are AWS benefits, speed and agility is the most direct answer to the scenario''s requirement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_33',
  'A global media company needs to deliver high-quality video content to users across continents with minimal latency. Their existing infrastructure struggles to provide consistent performance for viewers in distant regions. They are exploring AWS to improve the user experience by placing content and compute resources geographically closer to their diverse audience. Which aspect of the AWS Cloud''s value proposition directly addresses this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["The pay-as-you-go pricing model, reducing upfront capital expenditures.","The extensive global infrastructure, including Regions and Availability Zones.","The ability to achieve high availability and fault tolerance for critical workloads.","The elasticity to automatically scale resources up or down based on demand fluctuations."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'AWS''s extensive global infrastructure, comprising Regions, Availability Zones, and Edge Locations, allows customers to deploy applications and data geographically closer to their end-users. This significantly reduces latency and improves the user experience for a global audience, directly addressing the media company''s need. The pay-as-you-go model (Option 0) is a financial benefit. High availability and fault tolerance (Option 2) are reliability benefits. Elasticity (Option 3) is a scalability benefit. While all are AWS benefits, the global infrastructure is the direct answer to reducing latency for a global audience.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_34',
  'A small e-commerce business is experiencing rapid growth, leading to unpredictable spikes in website traffic during promotional events. Their current on-premises setup frequently crashes due to insufficient capacity, resulting in lost sales. They want to migrate to AWS to ensure their website can handle sudden increases in load without manual intervention or downtime, while only paying for the extra capacity when it''s actually needed. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud is most relevant to this business need?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to benefit from massive economies of scale, reducing infrastructure costs.","The option to trade fixed expenses for variable expenses, optimizing financial outflow.","The high availability and fault tolerance provided by AWS global infrastructure.","The elasticity and scalability to automatically adjust resources to meet demand."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Elasticity and scalability are key benefits of the AWS Cloud, allowing resources to be automatically provisioned and de-provisioned based on demand. This directly addresses the e-commerce business''s need to handle unpredictable traffic spikes without crashing and only pay for the additional capacity when it''s utilized. Economies of scale (Option 0) and trading fixed for variable expenses (Option 1) are cost benefits, while high availability and fault tolerance (Option 2) are reliability benefits. While these are important, elasticity and scalability directly solve the problem of handling fluctuating load efficiently.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_35',
  'A research institution frequently runs large-scale computational simulations that require significant compute power for short, intense periods. Historically, they''ve purchased and maintained powerful on-premises clusters that sit idle for much of the year, leading to inefficient capital utilization. They want to leverage AWS to access powerful resources only when needed for these simulations, thereby reducing their overall infrastructure expenditure. Which AWS Cloud benefit is most aligned with this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to deploy globally in minutes, enhancing collaboration across research teams.","The benefit of high availability, ensuring simulations are not interrupted by hardware failures.","The pay-as-you-go model, allowing payment only for consumed resources.","Increased speed and agility, enabling faster setup of new research environments."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The pay-as-you-go model is a fundamental benefit of cloud computing, allowing users to pay only for the resources they actually consume. This directly addresses the research institution''s need to access powerful compute resources for short periods without the large upfront investment and ongoing maintenance of idle hardware, thus reducing overall expenditure. Deploying globally (Option 0) is a geographic benefit. High availability (Option 1) is a reliability benefit. Speed and agility (Option 3) is an operational benefit. While these are all AWS benefits, the pay-as-you-go model is the most direct answer to the specific cost optimization scenario.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_36',
  'An organization is building a new application that requires extremely low latency access for users located across North America, Europe, and Asia. They want to ensure that their application''s performance is consistent and responsive for all users, regardless of their geographical location. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud''s global infrastructure is most crucial for achieving this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to leverage massive economies of scale for cost savings.","The high availability provided by deploying across multiple Availability Zones.","The extensive network of AWS Regions and Availability Zones.","The flexibility to trade capital expenses for variable expenses."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'AWS''s extensive network of Regions and Availability Zones allows organizations to deploy their applications and data geographically closer to their end-users. This proximity significantly reduces network latency, ensuring a consistent and responsive experience for users across different continents. Economies of scale (Option 0) are a cost benefit. High availability (Option 1) focuses on resilience within a region. Trading capital for variable expenses (Option 3) is a financial benefit. While all are AWS benefits, the global network of Regions and AZs directly addresses the low-latency requirement for a geographically dispersed user base.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_37',
  'A development team is frequently experimenting with new application features, requiring them to provision and de-provision development and testing environments multiple times a day. Their current on-premises setup makes this process slow and cumbersome, hindering innovation. They want to move to AWS to enable rapid provisioning of these environments, allowing them to iterate quickly and fail fast without significant cost implications. Which core benefit of the AWS Cloud supports this need for rapid experimentation?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to benefit from massive economies of scale, reducing the cost per unit.","The high availability and fault tolerance of the AWS global infrastructure.","The increased speed and agility in provisioning and de-provisioning resources.","The pay-as-you-go pricing model, eliminating upfront infrastructure investments."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Increased speed and agility is a key benefit of the AWS Cloud, allowing users to rapidly provision and de-provision resources. This enables development teams to quickly spin up and tear down environments for experimentation, fostering innovation and reducing the time required to test new ideas. Economies of scale (Option 0) are a cost benefit. High availability and fault tolerance (Option 1) are reliability benefits. The pay-as-you-go model (Option 3) is a financial benefit. While all are AWS benefits, speed and agility directly addresses the need for rapid experimentation and iteration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_38',
  'A company is designing a new critical application that must remain operational even if an entire data center experiences an outage. They plan to use AWS to achieve this high level of resilience. Which architectural principle, enabled by AWS''s global infrastructure, directly supports this requirement for continuous availability?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to trade capital expenses for variable expenses, optimizing financial outlay.","The benefit of massive economies of scale, reducing the overall cost of services.","High availability and fault tolerance through deployment across multiple Availability Zones.","Increased speed and agility, allowing rapid provisioning of resources for development."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'High availability and fault tolerance are achieved in AWS by designing applications to distribute resources across multiple Availability Zones within a Region. Each Availability Zone is an isolated location within a Region, designed to be independent from failures in other Availability Zones. This ensures that if one data center (Availability Zone) experiences an outage, the application remains operational, directly addressing the requirement for continuous availability. Trading CapEx for OpEx (Option 0) is a financial benefit. Economies of scale (Option 1) are a cost benefit. Speed and agility (Option 3) are operational benefits.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_39',
  'An organization is looking to reduce the administrative burden of managing their IT infrastructure, including tasks like hardware maintenance, patching, and operating system updates. They want to shift these responsibilities to a cloud provider so their internal IT team can focus on higher-value business initiatives. Which aspect of the AWS Cloud value proposition is most relevant to this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to deploy globally in minutes, expanding market reach.","The benefit of massive economies of scale, leading to lower pricing for services.","Reduced operational overhead by leveraging managed services.","The elasticity to automatically scale resources up or down based on demand."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Leveraging managed services in AWS significantly reduces operational overhead by shifting the responsibility for underlying infrastructure management (like hardware, OS, patching) to AWS. This allows the organization''s IT team to focus on higher-value tasks, directly addressing the goal of reducing administrative burden. Deploying globally (Option 0) is a geographic benefit. Economies of scale (Option 1) are a cost benefit. Elasticity (Option 3) is a scalability benefit. While all are AWS benefits, reduced operational overhead through managed services is the most direct answer to minimizing administrative burden.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_40',
  'A company is developing a new mobile application and needs to quickly provision backend services without going through lengthy procurement processes for hardware or software. They require the ability to experiment with different configurations and scale resources up or down frequently based on testing needs. Which benefit of the AWS Cloud is most impactful for their development velocity and ability to innovate?',
  'mcq',
  '["The high availability and fault tolerance, ensuring application uptime.","The global infrastructure, allowing deployment close to users worldwide.","The ability to increase speed and agility, accelerating development cycles.","The pay-as-you-go model, eliminating upfront capital expenditures."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Increased speed and agility allows developers to provision and de-provision resources rapidly, enabling quick experimentation and iteration on new features without the delays associated with traditional infrastructure procurement. This directly boosts development velocity and innovation. High availability (Option 0) is a reliability benefit. Global infrastructure (Option 1) is a geographic benefit. The pay-as-you-go model (Option 3) is a financial benefit. While all are AWS benefits, speed and agility is the most direct answer to the scenario''s focus on rapid development and experimentation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_41',
  'A startup is launching a new social media application and anticipates rapid, unpredictable user growth. They need an infrastructure that can handle fluctuating demand efficiently without requiring large upfront investments in hardware. The primary goal is to minimize the cost per user as their user base expands significantly, benefiting from the cloud''s inherent advantages.',
  'mcq',
  '["Leveraging AWS''s ability to aggregate demand from millions of customers, leading to lower pay-as-you-go pricing for compute and storage services.","Investing in a large on-premises data center to handle peak capacity, ensuring immediate availability for all users.","Purchasing Reserved Instances for all anticipated future capacity to secure the lowest possible hourly rates.","Migrating only a portion of the application to AWS while keeping the core database on-premises to reduce data transfer costs."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'The correct answer is leveraging AWS''s ability to aggregate demand from millions of customers, leading to lower pay-as-you-go pricing for compute and storage services. This describes the benefit of economies of scale, where AWS passes on the cost savings from its massive infrastructure to customers, resulting in lower prices as usage grows. Option B is incorrect because investing in a large on-premises data center represents a significant upfront capital expenditure and does not offer the pay-as-you-go flexibility or the immediate cost benefits of economies of scale (Anti-pattern: ap-1.1-001). Option C, purchasing Reserved Instances for all anticipated future capacity, might provide discounts but requires upfront commitment and can lead to over-provisioning if growth is unpredictable, negating the pay-as-you-go benefit (Anti-pattern: ap-1.1-004). Option D, migrating only a portion of the application, does not fully leverage the cloud''s benefits for scaling and cost efficiency for the entire application (Anti-pattern: ap-1.1-003).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_42',
  'A marketing department frequently launches new promotional campaigns, each requiring a dedicated web application and backend services that must be provisioned quickly and decommissioned just as fast. The team needs to reduce the time it takes to provision new environments from weeks to hours to respond rapidly to market opportunities and stay competitive.',
  'mcq',
  '["Maintaining a dedicated team of system administrators to manually configure new servers and network settings for each campaign.","Benefiting from the ability to rapidly provision and de-provision cloud resources on demand, allowing quick experimentation and deployment of new services.","Utilizing AWS''s global infrastructure to provision resources in multiple regions simultaneously, ensuring maximum redundancy.","Negotiating long-term contracts with hardware vendors to ensure a steady supply of physical servers for future campaigns."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The correct answer is benefiting from the ability to rapidly provision and de-provision cloud resources on demand, allowing quick experimentation and deployment of new services. This directly addresses the need for agility and speed, a core benefit of cloud computing, enabling businesses to innovate faster and respond to market changes. Option A is incorrect because manual configuration by a dedicated team is a slow, traditional approach that hinders agility (Anti-pattern: ap-1.1-002). Option C, utilizing global infrastructure for redundancy, is a benefit of AWS but does not directly address the speed of provisioning individual campaign environments. Option D, negotiating long-term hardware contracts, involves significant upfront commitment and does not offer the on-demand provisioning speed required for rapid campaign launches (Anti-pattern: ap-1.1-001).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_1_43',
  'A financial services company operates a critical online trading platform that must remain operational 24/7, even in the event of hardware failures or natural disasters affecting a single data center. They need to design their infrastructure to withstand such outages with minimal downtime and data loss to maintain customer trust and regulatory compliance.',
  'mcq',
  '["Replicating the entire application stack to an on-premises disaster recovery site located thousands of miles away.","Utilizing a single large Amazon EC2 instance to host all application services, ensuring all resources are co-located for performance.","Deploying all application components to a single AWS Region but across multiple Availability Zones.","Implementing a robust backup strategy for data, assuming that data recovery is sufficient for business continuity."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The correct answer is deploying all application components to a single AWS Region but across multiple Availability Zones. This strategy provides high availability and fault tolerance by distributing resources across physically isolated locations within a region, protecting against single data center outages. Option A, replicating to an on-premises DR site, is a valid strategy but does not leverage the inherent high availability features of AWS infrastructure within a region. Option B, utilizing a single large Amazon EC2 instance, creates a single point of failure and does not provide fault tolerance against hardware failures or data center outages (Anti-pattern: ap-1.2-004). Option D, implementing a robust backup strategy, is essential for data recovery but does not ensure minimal downtime for the application itself during an outage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- Module: m_60_4
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_26',
  'A financial services company is building a new transaction processing system on AWS. The system must be highly resilient, ensuring that a failure in one part of the application does not cause the entire system to become unavailable. They need to design the architecture so that components can operate and fail independently, minimizing the impact of any single point of failure and allowing for graceful degradation or recovery. Which AWS Well-Architected Framework design principle should be prioritized to meet this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating servers as pets, maintaining unique configurations for critical instances.","Decoupling components, using message queues or load balancers to isolate services.","Deploying all application components within a single Availability Zone for simplicity.","Focusing solely on cost optimization by using the smallest possible instance types."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Decoupling components is a core design principle for building resilient and fault-tolerant systems on AWS. By using mechanisms like message queues (e.g., Amazon SQS) or load balancers (e.g., Elastic Load Balancing), individual services can operate independently, and a failure in one component does not directly impact others, allowing for better fault isolation and scalability. Option 0 (Treating servers as pets) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-001) that contradicts the principle of disposable resources and makes systems less resilient and harder to scale. Option 2 (Deploying to a single Availability Zone) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-004) as it creates a single point of failure, making the system vulnerable to an AZ outage. Option 3 (Focusing solely on cost optimization) is a valid pillar but prioritizing it exclusively without considering reliability can lead to an unreliable system, which contradicts the primary requirement for resilience.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_27',
  'An online streaming service is migrating its legacy content processing workflow to AWS. The current on-premises system is a single, large application where a failure in any module, such as video encoding or thumbnail generation, can halt the entire pipeline, leading to service interruptions for users. The company wants to implement a cloud-native architecture that minimizes the impact of individual component failures and allows different parts of the workflow to operate and scale independently, ensuring continuous content delivery. Which AWS design principle should be prioritized to achieve this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Treating servers as pets by manually configuring and maintaining each Amazon EC2 instance for specific tasks.","Deploying all application components within a single Availability Zone to reduce network latency between them.","Decoupling components using message queues and load balancers, and distributing them across multiple Availability Zones.","Over-provisioning compute resources significantly to handle peak loads, even during periods of low demand, to ensure maximum performance."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option 2 (Decoupling components and distributing across multiple Availability Zones) is the correct answer. This approach aligns with the design principles of ''design for failure'' and ''decouple components,'' ensuring that a failure in one part of the system does not cascade and impact the entire workflow. Distributing across multiple Availability Zones further enhances reliability by protecting against AZ-wide outages. Option 0 (Treating servers as pets) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-001) that contradicts cloud-native principles of disposability and automation. Option 1 (Deploying to a single Availability Zone) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-004) as it creates a single point of failure and reduces fault tolerance. Option 3 (Over-provisioning compute resources) contradicts the principle of elasticity and cost optimization, as it leads to paying for idle capacity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_28',
  'A company is designing a mission-critical application on AWS that must withstand the failure of individual components or even an entire data center. They want to ensure that the application remains available and operational under these adverse conditions. Which design principle of the AWS Cloud should be prioritized to meet this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implementing elasticity to automatically scale resources based on demand.","Designing for failure, anticipating and mitigating potential outages.","Optimizing for cost efficiency by selecting the lowest-priced services.","Decoupling components to allow independent development and deployment."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Designing for failure is a core principle in the AWS Well-Architected Framework''s Reliability pillar. It involves anticipating that components will inevitably fail and designing systems to gracefully recover or continue operating without interruption, often by deploying across multiple Availability Zones. Implementing elasticity (Option 0) is for scalability. Optimizing for cost efficiency (Option 2) is a separate pillar. Decoupling components (Option 3) is a design principle that aids scalability and resilience but ''designing for failure'' is the overarching principle for fault tolerance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_29',
  'A company is developing a new application that processes customer orders. They want to ensure that if the order processing service temporarily fails or becomes overloaded, incoming orders are not lost and can be processed once the service recovers. Which AWS design principle should be applied to build a resilient system that handles intermittent failures gracefully?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implementing elasticity to scale the order processing service automatically.","Thinking parallel to process multiple orders concurrently for faster throughput.","Decoupling components, often using message queues, to absorb bursts and isolate failures.","Designing for disposable resources, allowing quick replacement of failed instances."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Decoupling components, typically by introducing message queues (like Amazon SQS) between services, allows the order submission service to place orders into a queue even if the processing service is unavailable or overloaded. The processing service can then consume messages from the queue when it is ready, ensuring no orders are lost and isolating the failure. Implementing elasticity (Option 0) focuses on scaling. Thinking parallel (Option 1) focuses on concurrency. Designing for disposable resources (Option 3) focuses on instance replacement. Decoupling directly addresses the need to handle intermittent failures gracefully without losing data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_30',
  'A company is developing a new application on AWS and wants to ensure that it adheres to best practices for security, reliability, and operational efficiency from the outset. They are looking for a comprehensive set of guidelines to help them design and operate their workloads effectively in the cloud. Which AWS resource provides this guidance?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Pricing Calculator, for estimating the cost of AWS services.","AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF), for guiding cloud migration strategies.","AWS Well-Architected Framework, providing prescriptive guidance across six pillars.","AWS Migration Hub, for tracking the progress of application migrations."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The AWS Well-Architected Framework provides a set of prescriptive guidelines and best practices across six pillars (Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization, and Sustainability) to help customers design and operate reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective workloads in the cloud. This directly addresses the need for comprehensive design and operational guidance. AWS Pricing Calculator (Option 0) is for cost estimation. AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (Option 1) is for migration strategy. AWS Migration Hub (Option 3) is for tracking migrations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_31',
  'A company is planning to deploy a new application that needs to handle varying loads throughout the day. They want to avoid over-provisioning resources during off-peak hours to save costs, but also ensure sufficient capacity during peak times. Which AWS design principle allows the system to automatically adjust its capacity to meet these fluctuating demands?',
  'mcq',
  '["Designing for failure to ensure resilience against component outages.","Implementing elasticity, allowing resources to scale in and out automatically.","Decoupling components to prevent cascading failures between services.","Thinking parallel to distribute workloads across multiple processing units."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Implementing elasticity is the design principle that enables systems to automatically scale resources up or down based on current demand. This allows the application to efficiently handle varying loads, ensuring cost savings during off-peak hours and sufficient capacity during peak times without manual intervention. Designing for failure (Option 0) focuses on resilience. Decoupling components (Option 2) focuses on isolation. Thinking parallel (Option 3) focuses on concurrency. Elasticity directly addresses the dynamic capacity adjustment for fluctuating demands.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_4_32',
  'A company is developing a new cloud-native application and wants to ensure that its architecture is robust, secure, and cost-effective. They are looking for a structured approach to evaluate their designs against AWS best practices. Which AWS tool or framework should they use to review their architecture and identify potential improvements?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Pricing Calculator, to estimate the costs of their proposed architecture.","AWS Migration Hub, to track the progress of their application migration.","AWS Well-Architected Tool, to review their architecture against best practices.","AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF), to guide their organizational cloud journey."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The AWS Well-Architected Tool allows users to review their architectures against the AWS Well-Architected Framework''s six pillars (Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization, and Sustainability). It helps identify high-risk issues and provides recommendations for improvement, directly addressing the need to evaluate designs against best practices. AWS Pricing Calculator (Option 0) is for cost estimation. AWS Migration Hub (Option 1) is for migration tracking. AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (Option 3) is for organizational cloud adoption strategy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  25,
