INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_34',
  'A company is planning a large-scale migration of its entire IT portfolio to the AWS Cloud. They recognize that this is not just a technical endeavor but also involves significant organizational change, skill development, and process adjustments. They need a structured approach to guide their transformation across various organizational capabilities to ensure a successful and sustainable cloud adoption. Which AWS framework provides guidance for this holistic approach?',
  'mcq',
  '["The AWS Well-Architected Framework, which provides best practices for designing and operating reliable, secure, efficient, and cost-effective systems.","The AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF), which helps organizations develop a comprehensive plan for cloud adoption across six perspectives.","The AWS Pricing Calculator, used to estimate the costs of various AWS services before committing to a migration strategy.","The AWS Migration Hub, which provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations from on-premises to AWS."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The scenario describes a need for a structured approach to guide organizational transformation, skill development, and process adjustments for cloud adoption. This holistic approach is the purpose of the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF). Option 1, ''The AWS Cloud Adoption Framework (AWS CAF), which helps organizations develop a comprehensive plan for cloud adoption across six perspectives,'' is the correct answer. Option 0, the AWS Well-Architected Framework, focuses on architectural best practices, not organizational change. Option 2, AWS Pricing Calculator, is for cost estimation. Option 3, AWS Migration Hub, is for tracking migration progress. This distractor represents anti-pattern `ap-1.3-003` if a candidate ignores organizational readiness.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_35',
  'A marketing department needs to quickly launch a new promotional website for an upcoming campaign. They require the ability to provision infrastructure rapidly, scale resources up or down based on campaign traffic, and deploy updates frequently without extensive lead times. The primary goal is to respond quickly to market demands and iterate on website features. Which benefit of migrating to the AWS Cloud is most relevant to this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to significantly reduce capital expenditures by converting them to operational expenses.","The improved agility and speed in provisioning resources and deploying applications, enabling faster time-to-market.","The enhanced business continuity through high availability and fault tolerance across multiple Availability Zones.","The benefit of massive economies of scale, leading to lower per-unit costs for cloud infrastructure services."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The scenario emphasizes rapidly provisioning infrastructure, scaling quickly, and deploying updates frequently to respond to market demands, which are all aspects of agility. Option 1, ''The improved agility and speed in provisioning resources and deploying applications, enabling faster time-to-market,'' directly addresses this. Option 0 describes the CapEx to OpEx financial benefit. Option 2 describes business continuity and fault tolerance. Option 3 describes economies of scale. While all are cloud benefits, agility is the most direct answer to the scenario''s requirements.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_36',
  'A company is migrating its legacy customer relationship management (CRM) application to AWS. The application uses a commercial database that requires specific licensing. The company wants to move the application to the cloud and take advantage of managed database services without re-architecting the entire application or changing the database engine. They are willing to make some minor modifications to the application to integrate with cloud services. Which migration strategy is most suitable?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost the application by moving the entire virtual machine, including the database, to Amazon EC2 without any changes.","Refactor the application by rewriting large portions of the code to use a serverless architecture with Amazon DynamoDB.","Replatform the application by moving it to Amazon EC2 and migrating the database to a compatible Amazon RDS instance.","Retain the application on-premises indefinitely because of the complexity of the commercial database licensing requirements."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The scenario describes moving to the cloud, taking advantage of managed database services, making minor modifications, and keeping the database engine. This aligns with the ''replatform'' strategy. Option 2, ''Replatform the application by moving it to Amazon EC2 and migrating the database to a compatible Amazon RDS instance,'' is the correct approach. Option 0, rehost, would not leverage managed database services. Option 1, refactor, involves significant code changes. Option 3, retain, means not migrating, which contradicts the goal. This distractor represents anti-pattern `ap-1.3-002` if a candidate only considers rehost without evaluating replatform for cloud-native benefits.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_37',
  'A company needs to migrate a large on-premises database (several terabytes) to Amazon RDS. They want to minimize downtime during the migration process and ensure data consistency between the source and target databases. The company requires a service that can facilitate a continuous replication of data while the migration is underway. Which AWS service is specifically designed to assist with this type of database migration?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Migration Hub, to centralize migration planning and track the overall progress of the project.","AWS Database Migration Service (DMS), to migrate databases with minimal downtime by continuously replicating data.","AWS Application Migration Service (AWS MGN), to lift and shift entire servers to AWS without application changes.","AWS Snowball, to physically transfer large amounts of data to AWS for offline migration."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'The scenario describes migrating a large database with minimal downtime and continuous data replication. AWS Database Migration Service (DMS) is specifically designed for this purpose. Option 1, ''AWS Database Migration Service (DMS), to migrate databases with minimal downtime by continuously replicating data,'' is the correct answer. Option 0, AWS Migration Hub, tracks migrations but doesn''t perform the data transfer. Option 2, AWS Application Migration Service, is for server migration, not specifically database replication. Option 3, AWS Snowball, is for offline physical data transfer, which might be part of a migration but not for continuous online replication.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_38',
  'A research institution has a massive dataset (hundreds of petabytes) stored on-premises that needs to be moved to Amazon S3 for long-term archival and analysis. Transferring this volume of data over the internet would take an unacceptably long time and incur high networking costs. The institution needs a secure and efficient way to physically transport this data to AWS. Which AWS service family is designed for large-scale data transfer using physical devices?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Database Migration Service (DMS) for migrating relational databases to AWS.","AWS Application Migration Service (AWS MGN) for rehosting physical servers to Amazon EC2.","The AWS Snow Family, including AWS Snowball and AWS Snowmobile, for petabyte-scale data transfer.","AWS Migration Hub, which provides a central location to track migration progress."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The scenario describes moving hundreds of petabytes of on-premises data to Amazon S3, emphasizing the need for secure and efficient physical transport due to the massive volume. The AWS Snow Family is specifically designed for this large-scale offline data transfer. Option 2, ''The AWS Snow Family, including AWS Snowball and AWS Snowmobile, for petabyte-scale data transfer,'' is the correct answer. Option 0, AWS DMS, is for database migration. Option 1, AWS Application Migration Service, is for server rehosting. Option 3, AWS Migration Hub, is for tracking, not data transfer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_39',
  'A company is planning to migrate several business-critical applications to the AWS Cloud. Before selecting specific migration strategies (like rehost or replatform), they need to understand the characteristics of each application, including its dependencies, performance requirements, compliance needs, and existing architecture. The company wants to avoid a ''one-size-fits-all'' approach that might lead to suboptimal outcomes. Which initial step is crucial for selecting the most effective migration strategy for each workload?',
  'mcq',
  '["Immediately refactoring all applications to a serverless architecture to maximize cloud-native benefits and agility.","Only considering the rehost (lift and shift) strategy for all applications to ensure the fastest possible migration timeline.","Assessing existing workloads thoroughly to understand their unique characteristics and dependencies before selecting a migration strategy.","Ignoring organizational readiness and technical skills, assuming the cloud migration will automatically resolve all existing IT challenges."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'The scenario emphasizes understanding the unique characteristics, dependencies, and requirements of each application before choosing a migration strategy to avoid suboptimal outcomes. Option 2, ''Assessing existing workloads thoroughly to understand their unique characteristics and dependencies before selecting a migration strategy,'' is the crucial initial step. Option 0, immediately refactoring everything, is an anti-pattern (`ap-1.3-001`) as it''s risky and slow. Option 1, only considering rehost, is an anti-pattern (`ap-1.3-002`) as it misses potential cloud-native benefits. Option 3, ignoring organizational readiness, is an anti-pattern (`ap-1.3-003`) that leads to migration failures. This distractor represents anti-pattern `ap-1.3-004` by not assessing existing workloads.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_40',
  'A company has several legacy applications running on aging on-premises servers. They need to quickly move these applications to AWS to reduce data center footprint and maintenance costs, but they have limited development resources and time for extensive code modifications. The primary objective is to achieve the fastest possible migration with minimal application changes.',
  'mcq',
  '["Refactoring all applications to use cloud-native services like AWS Lambda and Amazon DynamoDB, which requires significant code changes, extensive re-architecture, and considerable development effort over a long period.","Replatforming the applications to use managed services like Amazon RDS, requiring some code adjustments and compatibility testing to leverage cloud features.","Retiring the legacy applications and developing entirely new ones from scratch on AWS, which is the most extensive and time-consuming approach, often involving a complete business process re-evaluation.","Rehosting the applications to Amazon EC2 instances using tools like AWS Application Migration Service, without significant modifications to the application code."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'The ''rehost'' migration strategy, also known as ''lift and shift'', involves moving applications to AWS without making significant changes to their architecture or code. This is typically the fastest migration approach and requires minimal development resources, making Option 3 the correct choice. Option 0 (refactoring) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.3-001) as it requires extensive code changes and is not suitable for a fast migration with limited resources. Option 1 (replatforming) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.3-002) as it involves some modifications, making it slower than rehosting. Option 2 (retiring and redeveloping) is the most time-consuming and resource-intensive strategy, directly contradicting the requirement for the fastest migration with minimal changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_60_m_60_2_41',
  'A company has a critical, monolithic on-premises application that is stable but difficult to update and maintain due to its age. They need to migrate this application to AWS quickly to decommission their aging data center infrastructure and reduce operational costs. The development team has limited capacity for extensive code modifications in the short term, and the primary goal is to achieve cloud benefits with the LEAST amount of application code changes and the fastest possible transition time. Which migration strategy should the company prioritize?',
  'mcq',
  '["Replatforming the application by making minor modifications to integrate with AWS managed services like Amazon RDS and Amazon SQS.","Refactoring the application into a microservices architecture using AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS for cloud-native benefits.","Repurchasing a new Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) solution that provides equivalent business functionality to replace the existing application.","Rehosting the application by moving it to Amazon EC2 instances without significant modifications to the application code or architecture."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'The ''Rehost'' migration strategy, also known as ''lift and shift,'' involves moving an application to AWS with minimal or no changes to its architecture or code. This approach is typically the fastest way to migrate and requires the least amount of application code changes, directly meeting the company''s primary goal (Option D). Option A, Replatforming, involves some modifications to leverage cloud-native features, which requires more effort than rehosting. Option B, Refactoring, involves significant re-architecture and extensive code changes, which contradicts the requirement for the least amount of code changes and fastest transition, representing anti-pattern [ap-1.3-001]. Option C, Repurchasing, means replacing the existing application with a new SaaS solution, which is not a migration of the existing application and might involve significant business process changes and vendor lock-in.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain60_13',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_60_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

